<Layout title="Employment measures for aid beneficiaries | Spain 2026" description="Practical overview of Article 36 of Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 and its possible impact on certain employment decisions.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Legal updates · Business" title="Employment measures for certain companies receiving direct aid" description="What Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 changes and what a company should check before a sensitive employment decision." primaryLabel="Review our company situation" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Back to legal updates" secondaryHref="/en/legal-updates" note="Published: 30 September 2026 · Effective: 1 October 2026 · Primary source: BOE." />
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>What changes</h2><p>Article 36 of Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 establishes a temporary restriction for certain companies receiving direct aid and certain termination decisions connected with the situation covered by the measure.</p><h2>Who may be affected</h2><p>It does not apply to every company or every dismissal. The aid, employer, reason and date must be checked against the statutory wording. For permanent seasonal contracts, the rule also addresses ending an activity period or failing to call a worker back.</p><p>Article 36 provides specific consequences for a breach, including repayment of the aid and the dismissal being treated as null. Its application needs to be checked against the official wording and the facts.</p><p><a href="https://www.boe.es/buscar/act.php?id=BOE-A-2026-20265" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Royal Decree-Law 25/2026 at the BOE →</a></p></div></section><CTA title="Does this affect your company?" text="We can review the aid, the proposed measure and the documents before a decision is implemented." label="Contact the firm" /></Layout>
